-- Events in plain English: each sentence happens when the one before it has finished.
Let there be a flat video called events, 1080 by 1080, on #14121a, 5 s long.
Let there be a card called ball, of cardstock, 200 by 200, round, at 200 300.
Let there be a card called banner, of cardstock, 820 by 240, corners 40, at 540 760.
Write "It landed" called word in Lilita One, at 410 150, size 110.

Make the ball a radial gradient from #fff6c9 to #ff7a3d.
Make the banner a gradient from #3a1c71 to #d76d77 to #ffaf7b, angled 0.
Make the word white.

When the video reaches 0.5 s, move the ball to 880 300 over 1.4 s, bouncing.
When the ball arrives, change the banner to visible over 0.4 s.
When the banner appears, change the ball to 130% size for 0.3 s, then back.
When the banner appears, make the banner pulse, by 0.03, every 1.2 s.
When the video reaches 4.2 s, move the ball 300 down over 0.6 s.
